# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# AI Software Development Factory — .gitignore
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets / environment ---------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.keystore
*.jks
secrets.json
credentials.json
service-account*.json
.npmrc
.netrc

# --- Local Claude Code state --------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/local/
.claude-tmp/
.cc_tmp/

# --- OS / editor ---------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~

# --- Dependencies / build artifacts (for generated projects) --------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
.nuxt/
.svelte-kit/
coverage/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
target/
Pods/
.gradle/
*.apk
*.ipa
*.xcuserstate

# --- Test / tool output ---------------------------------------------
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
.playwright-mcp/
*.log
logs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated project output  (CLAUDE.md § 9 — two repositories)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything below belongs to the PRODUCT the factory builds, not to the
# factory itself. It stays on disk and stays fully resumable — `.project/state/`
# is read from the filesystem, never from git — but it is never committed to
# the factory repository.
#
# To give a generated project its own repository:
#     ./scripts/extract-project.sh ../my-project

# --- Manifest and run state -----------------------------------------
.project/

# --- Project agents generated by agent-generator ---------------------
# Note: project-state.md is a FACTORY agent (the state custodian), not a
# generated one. The naming collision is historical; keep the exception.
.claude/agents/project-*.md
!.claude/agents/project-state.md

# --- Platform source trees -------------------------------------------
/backend/
/web/
/mobile/
/shared/
/api/
/desktop/
/admin/
/integration/

# --- Evidence produced by real runs ----------------------------------
# The directory skeleton is kept; the artefacts are the project's.
evidence/*
!evidence/*/
evidence/*/*
!evidence/**/.gitkeep

# --- User-supplied source material ------------------------------------
# These are the project's inputs, and may be confidential.
/input/project-description.md
/input/references/*
!/input/references/.gitkeep

# --- Generated product documentation -----------------------------------
# docs/ holds BOTH factory documentation (committed) and generated product
# documentation (not committed). The generated names come from
# factory/templates/docs/*.template.md, plus the discovery capability profile.
/docs/PRD.md
/docs/acceptance-criteria.md
/docs/api-contract.md
/docs/architecture.md
/docs/assumptions.md
/docs/capability-profile.md
/docs/database-schema.md
/docs/deployment.md
/docs/design-system.md
/docs/development-plan.md
/docs/development-status.md
/docs/offline-sync.md
/docs/platform-requirements.md
/docs/project-overview.md
/docs/requirements.md
/docs/security.md
/docs/source-analysis.md
/docs/technology-stack.md
/docs/testing-strategy.md
/docs/user-stories.md

# --- Stray run artefacts at the repo root -------------------------------
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webm
/*.mp4
/*.zip
